<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernhard Rothmann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1495–c. 1535</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernhard Rothmann was a German preacher who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in the city of Münster, where he won much of the citizenry to Lutheran views by 1532. He then rejected infant baptism and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anabaptism">Anabaptists</a>, becoming the chief writer of the Anabaptist kingdom of Münster under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-matthys">Jan Matthys</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-leiden">Jan of Leiden</a>. He is thought to have died when the city fell in June 1535.</p></div>
